% ============================================================================
% mirror-focal-length-sign.query — worked recall queries against
% mirror-focal-length-sign.adj (adj-facts-stdlib, PHYSICS).
% ============================================================================
% Three queries: forward recall with citation, backward recall (bind a
% sign, find the mirror), and honest abstention on convex_lens (this
% table only grounds the two mirror types -- neither lens type has a
% sign convention stated in its own already-quoted span).
% ============================================================================

import "mirror-focal-length-sign.adj"

% Forward: what sign does the cited OpenStax span give for a concave mirror's focal length?
? mirror_focal_length_sign(concave_mirror, $Sign)

% Backward: which mirror has a negative focal length?
? mirror_focal_length_sign($Mirror, negative)

% Honest abstention: convex_lens's cited span describes ray behavior, not a sign convention.
? mirror_focal_length_sign(convex_lens, $SignLens)
